# Eight-point circle theorem — in a quadrilateral with perpendicular diagonals the four side midpoints are concyclic (source: Brand 1944; cut-the-knot)
A B C = triangle
E = foot(B, line(A, C))
D = on_line(B, E)
P = midpoint(A, B)
Q = midpoint(B, C)
R = midpoint(C, D)
S = midpoint(D, A)
prove cyclic(P, Q, R, S)
